window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-4abb15cbf2abe7df"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"create-or-revise-a-slide-deck\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">创建或修改演示文稿</h1> <p>将笔记、数据或现有演示文稿整理成幻灯片。</p> <p>根据源材料、参考演示文稿或可重复使用的模板，创建或修改 Google Slides 或 PowerPoint 演示文稿。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>将笔记、研究或数据整理成演示文稿。</li> <li>在保留结构和风格的同时更新现有演示文稿。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>presentations</code></td> <td>根据源材料、参考演示文稿或模板创建、编辑和预览 Google Slides 或 PowerPoint 演示文稿。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive（需联网）</a></td> <td>读取已连接的源文件，并创建或更新原生 Google Slides 演示文稿。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>template-creator</code></td> <td>将现有 PowerPoint 演示文稿转换为可重复使用的演示文稿模板。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>创建演示文稿</p> <p>建议模型：<code>gpt-6-astra</code> · 建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请使用 @Presentations，将我附上的材料整理成面向目标受众的演示文稿。\n\n如果我附上了现有演示文稿或模板，请匹配它的结构、视觉风格和品牌元素。尽可能让文字和图表保持可编辑；只有在能更清楚地表达要点时才使用视觉素材；并检查成品是否有版式或格式问题。请返回完成的演示文稿，并简要指出任何需要我复核的内容。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001278-creating-and-editing-documents-spreadsheets-and-presentations-with-chatgpt-work\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">使用 ChatGPT Work 创建和编辑文件（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001242\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT for PowerPoint（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"before-you-start\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">开始之前</h2> <p>先从现有材料着手：笔记、备忘录、研究、电子表格或已有演示文稿。告诉 ChatGPT 演示文稿面向谁、需要传达什么内容，以及哪些部分必须保持不变。</p> <p>在 ChatGPT 桌面应用中，使用 <code>@Presentations</code> 创建或编辑 PowerPoint 文件，或者根据源材料构建新的演示文稿。如果你想创建或更新原生 Google Slides，或引用 Google Workspace 中存储的文件，可以连接 Google Drive。你也可以直接附加本地文件。</p> <p>如果要在已打开的 PowerPoint 演示文稿中工作，请使用 <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001242\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT for PowerPoint（需联网）</a> 加载项。可用的插件、技能和已连接来源可能因套餐和工作区设置而异。</p> <p>在提示词中加入 <code>@Presentations</code>，即可查找模板库（Template Gallery）中保存的演示文稿模板。如果没有模板，Presentations 可以从内置版式开始，也可以参考现有演示文稿。</p> <p><a id=\"what-to-expect\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">你可以期待什么</h2> <p>ChatGPT 会先根据源材料整理一份简短的幻灯片计划，再制作演示文稿，并检查渲染后的幻灯片。它可以参考已有演示文稿或已保存的模板，保留已批准的数据和品牌元素，并标出需要来源依据的主张。</p> <p>下面是一次对话可能呈现的样子：</p> <p>ChatGPT 阅读了 Frontier Builders 的战略简报和审阅意见，为周一的领导层评审创建了一份六页演示文稿，制作了一张视觉化的开场页，并检查了版式问题。</p> <p>收到“让开场页更有视觉冲击力，并缩短决策页”的要求后，它调整了演示文稿，并返回更新后的版本。</p> <p>请检查最终幻灯片，而不只是大纲。确认叙述适合目标受众、主张和数字与来源材料一致，并且幻灯片易于阅读。进行大幅修改前，请复制重要演示文稿，以便需要时恢复。</p> <p><a id=\"make-it-work-for-you\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">按需调整</h2> <p>你可以使用后续提示词，让演示文稿匹配参考样式、适应新信息、面向不同受众，或将一种格式保存为以后可重复使用的模板。</p> <p><a id=\"save-the-format-as-a-reusable-template\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_9\">将格式保存为可重复使用的模板</h3> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $template-creator:template-creator to turn this presentation into a reusable template.\n\nPreserve the slide layouts, typography, colors, and brand elements so I can use this format for future [updates, reviews, or presentations].\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">使用 $template-creator:template-creator，将这个演示文稿转换成可复用模板。\n\n保留幻灯片布局、字体排版、颜色和品牌元素，让我以后可以将这种格式用于 [updates, reviews, or presentations]。</div></div> <p><a id=\"match-an-existing-presentation\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_10\">匹配现有演示文稿</h3> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use @Presentations to revise this deck to match [reference presentation].\n\nPreserve the reference layouts, typography, colors, logos, and section structure. Keep the current content and approved figures, and flag anything that doesn't fit cleanly.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">使用 @Presentations，修订这份幻灯片，使它与 [reference presentation] 一致。\n\n保留参考稿的布局、字体排版、颜色、Logo 和章节结构。保留当前内容和已批准的数字，并标出任何无法妥善融入的内容。</div></div> <p><a id=\"adapt-the-deck-for-a-different-audience\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_11\">为不同受众调整内容</h3> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Revise this presentation for [audience].\n\nMake the recommendation, supporting evidence, and next steps clear for them. Remove unnecessary detail, keep important figures intact, and preserve the existing style.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">请针对 [audience] 修改这份演示文稿。\n\n让他们能够清楚理解建议、支持证据和下一步行动。删除不必要的细节，完整保留重要数字，并保持现有风格。</div></div> <p><a id=\"update-the-deck-with-new-information\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_12\">用新信息更新演示文稿</h3> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Update this presentation using [new notes, spreadsheet, document, or connected source].\n\nIdentify which slides need to change, update the relevant claims and visuals, and leave unrelated slides untouched.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">请使用 [new notes, spreadsheet, document, or connected source] 更新这份演示文稿。\n\n找出需要修改的幻灯片，更新相关主张和视觉内容，不要改动无关的幻灯片。</div></div> <p>Template Creator 会将个人模板保存为基于原始演示文稿的模板，以便你在之后的任务中重复使用。高级图表、形状、格式或幻灯片管理操作，以及模板匹配，仍可能需要手动微调。分享前，请确认最终版式和主张。</p> <p>有关当前 Google Workspace 工作流程及受支持文件类型，请参阅<a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001278-creating-and-editing-documents-spreadsheets-and-presentations-with-chatgpt-work\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">使用 ChatGPT Work 创建和编辑文件（需联网）</a>；如需直接在已打开的文件中工作，请使用 <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001242\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT for PowerPoint（需联网）</a>。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"create-or-revise-a-slide-deck\">Create or revise a slide deck</h1> <p>Turn notes, data, or an existing presentation into a slide deck.</p> <p>Create or revise a Google Slides or PowerPoint presentation from source material, a reference deck, or a reusable template.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Turning notes, research, or data into a presentation.</li> <li>Refreshing an existing deck while preserving its structure and style.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>presentations</code></td> <td>Create, edit, and preview Google Slides or PowerPoint presentations from source material, a reference deck, or a template.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://github.com/openai/plugins/tree/main/plugins/google-drive\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">google-drive (online)</a></td> <td>Read connected source files and create or update native Google Slides presentations.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>template-creator</code></td> <td>Turn an existing PowerPoint presentation into a reusable presentation template.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Create a slide deck</p> <p>Suggested model：<code>gpt-6-astra</code> · Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use @Presentations to turn the material I've attached into a presentation for its intended audience.\n\nIf I've included an existing deck or template, match its structure, visual style, and branding. Keep text and charts editable where possible, use visuals when they make the point clearer, and check the finished slides for layout or formatting issues. Return the completed presentation and briefly flag anything that needs my review.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001278-creating-and-editing-documents-spreadsheets-and-presentations-with-chatgpt-work\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Create and edit files with ChatGPT Work (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001242\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT for PowerPoint (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"before-you-start\">Before you start</h2> <p>Start with the material you already have: notes, a memo, research, a spreadsheet, or an existing presentation. Tell ChatGPT who the deck is for, what it needs to communicate, and what should stay unchanged.</p> <p>In the ChatGPT desktop app, use <code>@Presentations</code> to create or edit a PowerPoint file or build a new presentation from your source material. Connect Google Drive when you want to create or update native Google Slides or reference files stored in Google Workspace. You can also attach local files directly.</p> <p>To work inside an open PowerPoint presentation, use the <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001242\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT for PowerPoint (online)</a> add-in. Available plugins, skills, and connected sources can vary by plan and workspace.</p> <p>Add <code>@Presentations</code> to your prompt to find saved presentation templates in the Template Gallery. If you don't have a template, Presentations can start from a built-in layout or follow an existing deck.</p> <h2 id=\"what-to-expect\">What to expect</h2> <p>ChatGPT turns the source material into a short slide plan, builds the presentation, and checks the rendered slides before returning the deck. It can follow a reference presentation or saved template, preserve approved figures and branding, and flag claims that need a source.</p> <p>Here is what that conversation can look like:</p> <p>ChatGPT reviewed the Frontier Builders strategy brief and review notes, created a six-slide presentation for Monday's leadership review, generated a visual opener, and checked the slides for layout issues.</p> <p>After a request to make the opener more visual and shorten the decision slide, it refined the deck and returned the updated presentation.</p> <p>Review the final slides, not only the outline. Check that the story fits the audience, the claims and numbers match the source material, and the slides are readable. Duplicate important decks before making large changes so you can revert if needed.</p> <h2 id=\"make-it-work-for-you\">Make it work for you</h2> <p>Use follow-on prompts to match a reference, adapt the story, bring in new information, or save a format you expect to use again.</p> <h3 id=\"save-the-format-as-a-reusable-template\">Save the format as a reusable template</h3> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use $template-creator:template-creator to turn this presentation into a reusable template.\n\nPreserve the slide layouts, typography, colors, and brand elements so I can use this format for future [updates, reviews, or presentations].\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"match-an-existing-presentation\">Match an existing presentation</h3> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use @Presentations to revise this deck to match [reference presentation].\n\nPreserve the reference layouts, typography, colors, logos, and section structure. Keep the current content and approved figures, and flag anything that doesn't fit cleanly.\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"adapt-the-deck-for-a-different-audience\">Adapt the deck for a different audience</h3> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Revise this presentation for [audience].\n\nMake the recommendation, supporting evidence, and next steps clear for them. Remove unnecessary detail, keep important figures intact, and preserve the existing style.\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"update-the-deck-with-new-information\">Update the deck with new information</h3> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Update this presentation using [new notes, spreadsheet, document, or connected source].\n\nIdentify which slides need to change, update the relevant claims and visuals, and leave unrelated slides untouched.\n</code></pre> <p>Template Creator saves a personal template backed by the original presentation, so you can reuse the same format in a future task. Template matching and advanced chart, shape, formatting, or slide-management edits can still need manual refinement. Confirm the final layout and claims before sharing.</p> <p>See <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001278-creating-and-editing-documents-spreadsheets-and-presentations-with-chatgpt-work\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Create and edit files with ChatGPT Work (online)</a> for the current Google Workspace workflow and supported file types, or use <a href=\"https://help.openai.com/en/articles/20001242\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">ChatGPT for PowerPoint (online)</a> to work directly in an open PowerPoint presentation.</p>"};
